# A store into a view of numbers converts what is stored. Of a value that nobody knows that may run code: the store tests the cell, the key and the value each turn, and nothing is taken in front of the loop.
# `value` comes from in front of the loop and every turn stores it: in the copy of the loop for each kind of view it is asked for a number once, in front, and the store is the proven one.
# What is no number runs the loop as it was. A list takes whatever comes: in its copy nothing is asked of `value`.
